## 1 · Endpoints

One per line. `operationId` is a contract: it becomes a method name in the generated client.
`Path` is the public URI a client calls; the controller's mapping carries the resource alone
(`/users`) and `Version` as its `version` attribute — the `/api/v{version}` prefix is § 7's
configuration. `1+` is a baseline: served at v1 and every later version until a mapping at a
higher one supersedes it.

| Method | Path | Version | `operationId` | Inbound port | Success |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `POST` | `/api/v1/users` | `1+` | `createUser` | `CreateUserUseCase` | 201 + `Location` + representation |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/users` | `1+` | `listUsers` | `ListUsersQuery` | 200 + page envelope |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/users/{userId}` | `1+` | `getUser` | `ListUsersQuery.byId` | 200 + representation |

No `PUT` nor `PATCH` in this iteration: the parent spec has no update use case.
Adding an endpoint with no use case behind it is guessing the contract.

`POST /api/v1/users` requires `Idempotency-Key`: it creates a resource. The `GET`s don't — they're safe.

## 2 · DTOs

| DTO | Direction | Fields | Shape validation |
|---|---|---|---|
| `CreateUserRequest` | input | `email`, `name`, `departmentId?` | `@NotBlank` + `@Email` + `@Size(max=254)`; `name` `@NotBlank` + `@Size(max=120)` |
| `UserResponse` | output | `id`, `email`, `name`, `createdAt` | — |
| `PageResponse<UserResponse>` | output | `content`, `page{number,size,totalElements,totalPages}` | — |

Validation here is **shape** only. "Email already registered" isn't `@Email`: it's an
aggregate invariant, lives in `10-dominio.md`, and comes out as 422 — see block 3.

DTO ↔ domain translation in `UserMapper`, static methods, manual. The DTO's `String`
becomes `Email` in the mapper and nowhere else.

## 3 · Error map

Each exception from `10-dominio.md`, its status, and the `errorCode` the client sees. This
table is the source of block 5 — no test case comes from anywhere but here.

| Situation | Domain exception | Status | `errorCode` | Extra fields |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Email already registered | `BusinessRuleViolationException` | 422 | `EMAIL_ALREADY_REGISTERED` | `errorCode` |
| Given department doesn't exist | `NotFoundException` | 404 | `DEPARTMENT_NOT_FOUND` | `errorCode` |
| Unknown `userId` in `GET` | `NotFoundException` | 404 | `USER_NOT_FOUND` | `errorCode` |
| Same key, different body | `ConflictException` | 409 | `IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED` | `errorCode` |
| `Idempotency-Key` missing or malformed | — (`MissingIdempotencyKeyException`, structural) | 400 | **none** | `violations` |
| API version outside the supported list | — (`InvalidApiVersionException`, structural) | 400 | **none** | `violations` on `version` |
| Required field missing, malformed `email` | — (bean validation) | 400 | **none** | `violations` |
| Unreadable JSON, incompatible type | — (deserialization) | 400 | **none** | — |
| Unmapped | — | 500 | **none** | `traceId` |

Bean validation never carries `errorCode`: it's structural, not from the domain.
`traceId` comes from Micrometer Tracing, `Tracer` injected into `ApiExceptionHandler`.

## 4 · Pagination, idempotency, and dependencies

**Pagination** — `GET /api/v1/users` is offset: `page` (0-based), `size` defaulting to 20
and capped at 100, `sort` defaulting to `createdAt,desc`. Tiebreak by `id` is mandatory,
added in the application and not requested from the client. Cursor isn't used here: the
expected volume (~200,000 rows in 12 months, answered in this skill's interview) doesn't
justify it.

**Idempotency** — two halves, and only the first belongs to this partial:

| Half | Where it lives | In this partial |
|---|---|---|
| Header presence and format | `IdempotencyKeyInterceptor` in the adapter | yes — 400 above |
| Claim (own transaction), then effect + stored response (one transaction) | `IdempotentExecution`, application layer, called by the controller; the command carries no key | no — only declared as needed |
| `idempotency_keys` table (route, caller, body hash, status, body, lease, TTL >= 24 h) | `20-persistencia.md` | no — **handed off to `persistence-architect`** |

**Schema requirements** — read by `persistence-architect` in its first pass, which runs
after this partial:

| Requirement | Why |
|---|---|
| `idempotency_keys` table, shared — reuse if it already exists | `POST /api/v1/users` requires `Idempotency-Key` (`api-rest.md` § Idempotency) |
| `users` expected volume: ~200,000 rows in 12 months | decides offset pagination here; sizes indexes there |

**Dependencies to add** — the executor applies them to `pom.xml`; this skill only
declares them.

| Artifact | Why | Version |
|---|---|---|
| `org.springdoc:springdoc-openapi-starter-webmvc-ui` | Generates `openapi.json` from the code | **not managed by the Spring Boot BOM** — resolve at runtime, never from memory |
| `io.micrometer:micrometer-tracing-bridge-otel` | Source of `traceId` | managed by the BOM |
| `spring-boot-starter-validation` | Bean validation on the DTOs | managed by the BOM |

## 5 · Contract test cases

What the test has to assert. **The test code comes from the executor**, not this skill.
Asserting only the status number isn't enough: a wrong `errorCode` would slip through.

| Case | Request | Asserts |
|---|---|---|
| Happy creation | valid `POST` + key | 201, `Location` header present, `email` in the body |
| Business rule | `POST` with an already-registered email | 422 **and** `errorCode = EMAIL_ALREADY_REGISTERED` |
| Invalid shape | `POST` without `email` | 400, `violations[0].field = email`, `errorCode` absent |
| Missing key | `POST` without `Idempotency-Key` | 400 |
| Idempotency | two identical `POST`s with the same key | only one user created, two identical responses, same status |
| Reused key | same key, different body | 409 **and** `errorCode = IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED` |
| Empty page | `GET` with no results | 200 with `content: []` — never 204 |
| Stable ordering | `GET` page 0 and page 1 | empty intersection |
| `size` above the maximum | `GET ?size=500` | 400 — never truncated silently |
| Unsupported API version | `GET /api/v99/users` | 400, `violations[0].field = version`, `errorCode` absent — first REST case of the project only |

Body-shape fixtures: `templates/error-responses.json.example` and
`templates/page-response.json.example`.

## 6 · Personal data

none

Every field of a **response** body above that matches the derivation in
`@.claude/rules/logging.md` § Masking candidates. Run `@.claude/rules/personal-data.md` § How to
verify grep 1 against the DTOs this partial designed and read the hits against that list;
`none` is a decision, absence is a gap.

`@MaskSensitiveData` on the DTO does not answer this block. Masking covers the log line; this
block covers the body that leaves the process, and a field masked in the logs and returned in
clear was never protected — it was protected in the one place someone happened to look
(`@.claude/rules/personal-data.md`, opening principle).

| Field | Form | Receiver and reason |
|---|---|---|
| `customer.document` (CPF) | reduced — last 4 digits | The screen only disambiguates between two accounts; nothing downstream needs the full value |

A **full value** carries the receiver's name and the reason, and without them consolidation
stops. `reduced` and `reference` need no receiver column: nothing personal crosses.

## 7 · Versioning

`@.claude/rules/api-rest.md` § Versioning. The project setup is written once, by the first
REST case of the project (NEW); every later case writes `inherited from UC-NNN` in its place
and fills only **Changes in this case**.

**Project setup** — NEW in this case: no `ApiVersioningConfig` exists yet.

| Setting | Value |
|---|---|
| Strategy | Path segment: prefix `/api/v{version}` on the REST adapter package's controllers, read only under `/api/` — `ApiVersioningConfig` |
| Supported versions | `1` |
| Required | yes, no default version |
| Deprecated versions | none |
| Use per version | `api.version` tag on `http.server.requests` — `ApiVersionObservationConvention` |

**Changes in this case** — none.

A later case that changes an existing endpoint in a way `api-rest.md` § Versioning calls
breaking writes one row per change, and the executor CHANGEs `ApiVersioningConfig`:

`| Change | Version | Endpoints | Dates | Justification |`

- *New version* — `2` added to the supported list; the endpoints that break get a mapping at
  `2+` beside the `1+` one, which stays; every other endpoint reaches v2 through its baseline.
  The breaking change that forces it goes in Justification.
- *Deprecation* — `Deprecation` and `Sunset` dates for the old version, and the link to the
  migration notes, which also say that operations reached through a baseline are listed in
  the OpenAPI document under their starting version only. Justification: the measured use of
  that version (`api.version`), and the consumers known to call it.
- *Sunset* — the version leaves the supported list and its mappings are deleted, in the same
  change. Never before the `Sunset` date recorded when it was deprecated.

## 8 · Admission

none — `00-caso-de-uso.md`'s `Admission` row is `none`: the request states no quota and no cap.

`@.claude/rules/inbound-admission.md`. A case whose row states a limit fills two parts. The
**project setup** is written once, by the first case with a limit (NEW); every later case writes
`inherited from UC-NNN` in its place, or the row it adds as a CHANGE:

| Setting | Value — shape |
|---|---|
| Quota enforced | `application` — `AdmissionConfig` registers the interceptor · or `edge: <ingress or gateway>` — no limiter written; the number and the key below are what the edge enforces, and no test here proves them |
| Replicas | `3` in production — each quota below is divided by it, rounded up |
| Caller's key | from `Access`: the principal's name · the API key's id · the client address (public endpoint; forwarded headers only with the trusted proxies of the root `CLAUDE.md`'s `**Transport:` paragraph) |
| Wait on 503 | `1 s` — `app.admission.busy-retry-after`; why: the slowest call the cap guards answers in ~800 ms p99 |
| Limiter cache | `app.admission.max-clients: 10000` callers, expiry after access = the longest window |

**Limits of this case** — the executor writes `@InboundQuota` and `@Bulkhead` on the handler
method, and their entries in `application.yml`:

`| Limit | Name | Stated | Per replica | Window or size | Reason |`

- *Quota* — name `uc-104-search-orders` (the case slug), stated `100 per minute per client`,
  per replica `34`, window `1m`. Block 3 gains `quota spent → 429 RATE_LIMITED, Retry-After 60`;
  block 5 the case that spends it and the case of another caller who keeps theirs
- *Cap* — name `inbound-uc-104-search-orders`, stated `20 at the same time`, size `20`, no wait;
  reason: below the 200 request threads, with the provider call it holds measured at ~800 ms.
  Block 3 gains `cap full → 503 SERVICE_BUSY, Retry-After` and `traceId`; block 5 the case that
  fills it and asserts no idempotency key was claimed

## Design patterns

none — no force in the spec, no symptom on disk

One row per pattern this layer adopts, decided through
`@.claude/skills/gof-design-patterns/SKILL.md` § Design-time use:
`| Force or symptom | Pattern | Classes and interfaces it creates | "When not" checked |`.
The force is a spec line or a `file:line`, never "might grow". Every class a row creates is
also listed where this partial lists what the executor writes; reshaping code an approved
case produced is a row in the section below. Consolidation collects this section into
`UC-NNN-spec.md`.

